# =============================================================================
# BUILD 03 (FAILED ATTEMPT): Relational Joins, Constraints & Atomic Checkout
# =============================================================================

Wallets is a collection.
Each wallet has a wallet_id (text), a balance (number) and a frozen (number).
No two wallets share the same wallet_id.
If a wallet already exists, reject it.

Products is a collection.
Each product has a sku (text), a price (number) and a stock (number).
No two products share the same sku.
If a product already exists, reject it.

Purchases is a collection.
Each purchase has a purchase_id (number), a buyer_wallet (text), a item_sku (text) and a total_cost (number).
No two purchases share the same purchase_id.
If a purchase already exists, reject it.

# FAILURE 1: Cross-collection sentence (referencing two collections in one sentence)
# Rejected by parser.py:468: "one sentence can only be about one collection in this version"
checkout-join: show the purchases and wallets whose wallet_id is buyer_wallet.

# FAILURE 2: Domain invariant constraint ("stock is never under 0")
# Misread as a task or fails with unknown word "never"
Products whose stock is never under 0.

# FAILURE 3: Combining an action ("show") and a state change ("decrease") in one capability
# Rejected by parser.py:937: "is this a change or a query?"
buy-and-receipt: decrease stock by a given qty and show the product for products whose sku is a given sku.

# FAILURE 4: Bulk update of a unique property (purchase_id)
# Rejected by check.py:157: "changing 'purchase_id' in bulk is not supported yet because it is unique"
renumber-purchases: increase purchase_id by 1000 for every purchase.

# FAILURE 5: Teaching a phrase with "is" instead of "whose ... is" or "equal to"
# Because "is" is tokenized as ('IS', None) rather than ('CMP', 'eq'), parser.py:942
# fails to split a bare condition without "whose" when the comparison uses "is"!
"frozen_acct" means frozen is 1.
show-frozen: show the wallet_id of wallets frozen_acct.

